// Title: Remote Access Tool - AnyDesk Piped Password Via CLI
// Sigma ID: b1377339-fda6-477a-b455-ac0923f9ec2c
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-09-28 | Modified: 2023-03-05
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1219.002
// Description: Detects piping the password to an anydesk instance via CMD and the '--set-password' flag.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate piping of the password to anydesk
//   - Some FP could occur with similar tools that uses the same command line '--set-password'
// References:
//   - https://redcanary.com/blog/misbehaving-rats/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_remote_access_tools_anydesk_piped_password_via_cli.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "/c " and ProcessCommandLine contains "echo " and ProcessCommandLine contains ".exe --set-password"
